    "reason": "The English lemma 'boundary' primarily refers to the dividing line or limit of an area. The Japanese expression '区域' (kuiki) primarily means 'area' or 'zone', which is the space itself, rather than the demarcation line. While '区域' implies an area with limits, it does not directly translate to the 'boundary' (the line) itself. Therefore, '区域' is semantically broader than 'boundary'. A more direct and natural translation for 'boundary' (the line/limit) would be '境界' or '境界線'.",
